        <strong>ORL proves that autoregressive decoding is not the only path to high-quality text generation.</strong> 2,788 tokens per second on a single consumer GPU, matching GPT-6 Luna quality on hard reasoning benchmarks, with linear multi-GPU scaling. The 3B and 8B checkpoints are open-sourced by a collaboration between Cambridge, EPFL, Anthropic, and Mistral. <strong>If this architecture scales to larger models, the autoregressive paradigm that every major LLM is built on becomes the slow, expensive option.</strong> Paper: <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.17894" class="text-violet-400 hover:underline">arXiv 2610.17894</a>.
